An extra factor of I supplied by a vertex remains a separate coefficient."}],
   "Notes"], Cell[TextData[{"Generator loops of any length become ordered \
traces. The SU(3) completeness identity contracts a repeated adjoint dummy \
between generators or traces. Hermitian conjugation swaps a generator's two \
fundamental slots, while conjugating a trace reverses its order. This also \
lets ", ButtonBox["SquareAmplitude", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/SquareAmplitude"],
     " form the correct conjugate color expression."}], "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[
    {"A repeated symbolic dummy label is summed, but an external ",
     ButtonBox["ColorIndex", BaseStyle -> "Link",
      ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/ref/ColorIndex"], " remains a free \
external color label by default. Literal positive integer indices are fixed \
matrix components, not dummy summation labels. A dummy used more than twice \
in one term is an invalid Einstein contraction and is reported explicitly."}]\
, "Notes"], Cell[TextData[{"Use ",
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"SumExternalColors\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]],
      "InlineFormula"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{" ", "on", " ", "a", " ",
